## Brazil

nucleo-pais-br-extras = 13º salary and vacation bonus (one third)
nucleo-pais-br-holerite = payslip
nucleo-pais-br-holerites = payslips
nucleo-pais-br-tipo-clt = CLT
nucleo-pais-br-tipo-pj = PJ
nucleo-pais-br-dica-1 = An emergency fund of 6 months of essential spending, somewhere with daily liquidity (Tesouro Selic or a daily-liquidity CDB paying close to 100% of the CDI).
nucleo-pais-br-dica-2 = With a fixed income, set your savings aside on payday (pay yourself first); with a variable income, plan around the weak month.
nucleo-pais-br-dica-3 = 13º and vacation pay: decide in advance where they go (expensive debt, emergency fund, goals).
nucleo-pais-br-dica-4 = Retirement: the INSS is the base; a PGBL only pays off if you file the full income tax return (it deducts up to 12% of taxable income).

## United States

nucleo-pais-us-contribuicao = Social Security and Medicare (FICA)
nucleo-pais-us-imposto = Federal income tax withheld
nucleo-pais-us-recibo = paystub
nucleo-pais-us-recibos = paystubs
nucleo-pais-us-tipo-empregado = Employee (W-2)
nucleo-pais-us-tipo-aposentadoria = Retirement (Social Security, pension)
nucleo-pais-us-tipo-contractor = Contractor (1099)
nucleo-pais-us-tipo-autonomo = Self-employed
nucleo-pais-us-tipo-informal = Informal (gig work)
nucleo-pais-us-tipo-beneficio = Benefits (SNAP, unemployment)
nucleo-pais-us-dica-1 = Emergency fund: 3 to 6 months of essential spending in a high-yield savings account or a money market fund.
nucleo-pais-us-dica-2 = 401(k): contribute at least enough to get the full employer match; it's money you lose if you leave it on the table.
nucleo-pais-us-dica-3 = An IRA or Roth IRA if you don't have a 401(k) or already get the match; a Roth is worth more when your tax rate today is low.
nucleo-pais-us-dica-4 = Pay your credit card in full every month: revolving interest is over 20% a year and drags down your credit score.
nucleo-pais-regra-50-30-20 = The 50/30/20 rule as a starting point: 50% needs, 30% wants, 20% savings and debt.
nucleo-pais-us-limite-1 = State and local income taxes aren't included in payroll deductions (only federal tax and FICA).
nucleo-pais-us-limite-2 = Federal tax is estimated as a single filer, with the standard deduction.
nucleo-pais-us-limite-3 = The app doesn't calculate tax on investments (forms 1099 and 8949).

## Portugal

nucleo-pais-pt-inflacao = HICP
nucleo-pais-pt-imposto = IRS withheld
nucleo-pais-pt-extras = Holiday and Christmas allowances
nucleo-pais-pt-recibo = payslip
nucleo-pais-pt-recibos = payslips
nucleo-pais-pt-tipo-conta-de-outrem = Employee
nucleo-pais-pt-tipo-funcao-publica = Civil service
nucleo-pais-pt-tipo-reforma = Retirement
nucleo-pais-pt-tipo-independente = Self-employed worker (recibos verdes)
nucleo-pais-pt-tipo-conta-propria = Own business
nucleo-pais-pt-tipo-rendas = Rental income
nucleo-pais-pt-tipo-prestacao = Social benefit (abono, RSI, unemployment)
nucleo-pais-pt-dica-1 = An emergency fund of 6 months of essential expenses, in an instant-access term deposit or in Certificados de Aforro.
nucleo-pais-pt-dica-2 = Holiday and Christmas allowances: decide in advance where they go (debt, emergency fund, goals) instead of spending them that month.
nucleo-pais-pt-dica-3 = PPR: besides saving for retirement, 20% of what you put in during the year is deducted from your IRS, with a cap by age.
nucleo-pais-pt-dica-4 = A variable-rate mortgage follows the Euribor: simulate the payment with the highest rate before deciding.
nucleo-pais-pt-limite-1 = IRS withholding is estimated from the annual tax (mainland brackets), not from the monthly withholding tables.
nucleo-pais-pt-limite-2 = The Azores and Madeira have their own IRS and VAT rates, which the app doesn't apply.
nucleo-pais-pt-limite-3 = The app doesn't prepare the IRS return (Modelo 3) or calculate capital gains.
nucleo-pais-es-inflacao = HICP
nucleo-pais-es-imposto = IRPF withheld
nucleo-pais-es-extras = June and December extra pay
nucleo-pais-es-recibo = nómina
nucleo-pais-es-recibos = nóminas
nucleo-pais-es-tipo-cuenta-ajena = Employee
nucleo-pais-es-tipo-funcionario = Civil servant
nucleo-pais-es-tipo-jubilacion = Retirement pension
nucleo-pais-es-tipo-autonomo = Self-employed (invoices)
nucleo-pais-es-tipo-cuenta-propia = Own business
nucleo-pais-es-tipo-prestacion = Social benefit (unemployment, Ingreso Mínimo Vital)
nucleo-pais-es-dica-1 = Emergency fund of 6 months of essential expenses, in an interest-bearing account or Letras del Tesoro.
nucleo-pais-es-dica-2 = June and December extra pay: decide beforehand where it goes (debts, emergency fund, goals) instead of spending it that month.
nucleo-pais-es-dica-3 = Plan de pensiones: up to €1,500 a year comes off the IRPF base (plus up to €8,500 in an employer plan).
nucleo-pais-es-dica-4 = A variable-rate mortgage follows Euribor: simulate the payment at the highest rate before deciding.
nucleo-pais-es-limite-1 = IRPF is estimated with the general scale (state + common regional), not your region's scale or the withholding algorithm.
nucleo-pais-es-limite-2 = Navarre and the Basque Country (foral regime) and the Canary Islands (IGIC instead of VAT) have their own rules that the app does not apply.
nucleo-pais-es-limite-3 = The annual income tax return and capital gains are not calculated by the app.
nucleo-pais-gb-contribuicao = National Insurance
nucleo-pais-gb-imposto = Income Tax (PAYE)
nucleo-pais-gb-recibo = payslip
nucleo-pais-gb-recibos = payslips
nucleo-pais-gb-dica-1 = Emergency fund of at least 3 months of essential outgoings (MoneyHelper), in an easy-access savings account.
nucleo-pais-gb-dica-2 = ISA: up to £20,000 a year with tax-free returns; a Lifetime ISA helps with a first home or retirement.
nucleo-pais-gb-dica-3 = Workplace pension: contribute at least enough to get the full employer match.
nucleo-pais-gb-limite-1 = Uses the England, Wales and Northern Ireland bands: Scotland has its own income tax bands.
nucleo-pais-gb-limite-2 = The personal allowance taper above £100,000 and tax codes are not applied.
nucleo-pais-ca-contribuicao = CPP and EI
nucleo-pais-ca-imposto = Federal and provincial tax
nucleo-pais-ca-recibo = pay stub
nucleo-pais-ca-recibos = pay stubs
nucleo-pais-ca-dica-1 = Emergency fund of 3 to 6 months of expenses, in a high-interest savings account or a TFSA.
nucleo-pais-ca-dica-2 = RRSP: contributions come off taxable income (18% of last year's income, up to the limit); TFSA: up to CAD 7,000 a year with tax-free growth.
nucleo-pais-ca-dica-3 = FHSA: up to CAD 8,000 a year for a first home, deductible and tax-free when withdrawn.
nucleo-pais-ca-limite-1 = Taxes are calculated for Ontario; other provinces (and Quebec, with the QPP) have their own tables.
nucleo-pais-ca-limite-2 = The Ontario surtax, the Ontario Health Premium and the CPP and EI credits are not applied.
nucleo-pais-fr-contribuicao = Cotisations salariales
nucleo-pais-fr-imposto = Prélèvement à la source
nucleo-pais-fr-recibo = bulletin de paie
nucleo-pais-fr-recibos = bulletins de paie
nucleo-pais-fr-dica-1 = Precautionary savings of 3 to 6 months of expenses, in a Livret A or LDDS (tax-free).
nucleo-pais-fr-dica-2 = PER: contributions come off taxable income up to 10% of professional income (minimum €4,710).
nucleo-pais-fr-dica-3 = Assurance-vie and PEA: tax advantages after 8 and 5 years, respectively.
nucleo-pais-fr-limite-1 = Tax is estimated for one person (1 part): the family quotient for children and couples is not applied.
nucleo-pais-fr-limite-2 = Contributions are an average of ~22% for non-executive employees; your personalised withholding rate beats the estimate.
nucleo-pais-de-contribuicao = Sozialversicherung
nucleo-pais-de-imposto = Lohnsteuer
nucleo-pais-de-recibo = Lohnabrechnung
nucleo-pais-de-recibos = Lohnabrechnungen
nucleo-pais-de-dica-1 = Emergency fund of 3 to 6 net salaries in a Tagesgeldkonto (the Verbraucherzentrale suggests at least 2 to 3).
nucleo-pais-de-dica-2 = bAV (company pension): up to 8% of the pension ceiling tax-free, and 4% also free of social contributions.
nucleo-pais-de-dica-3 = ETF savings plan and Riester/Rürup: compare costs first; Riester has a state bonus per child.
nucleo-pais-de-limite-1 = Lohnsteuer is estimated for tax class I, without Solidaritätszuschlag, church tax or child allowance.
nucleo-pais-de-limite-2 = Long-term care insurance uses the rate for parents (1.8%); without children, from age 23, it is 2.4%.
nucleo-pais-ar-contribuicao = Contributions (jubilación, PAMI, obra social)
nucleo-pais-ar-imposto = Impuesto a las Ganancias
nucleo-pais-ar-recibo = recibo de sueldo
nucleo-pais-ar-recibos = recibos de sueldo
nucleo-pais-ar-extras = Aguinaldo (SAC) in June and December
nucleo-pais-ar-dica-1 = With high inflation, keep the emergency fund where it at least matches inflation (UVA fixed-term deposit or money-market FCI) and can be withdrawn quickly.
nucleo-pais-ar-dica-2 = Aguinaldo: decide beforehand where it goes (debts, emergency fund, goals) instead of spending it that month.
nucleo-pais-ar-dica-3 = Compare the total financial cost (CFT) before paying in card installments or taking a loan.
nucleo-pais-ar-limite-1 = Ganancias is estimated with the 2026 annual scale split into 13 payments, without the July update or deductions beyond the personal and per-child ones.
nucleo-pais-ar-limite-2 = The contribution ceiling changes every month: the app uses October 2026's.
nucleo-pais-cl-contribuicao = Cotizaciones (AFP, health, cesantía)
nucleo-pais-cl-imposto = Impuesto Único
nucleo-pais-cl-recibo = liquidación de sueldo
nucleo-pais-cl-recibos = liquidaciones de sueldo
nucleo-pais-cl-dica-1 = Emergency fund of 3 to 6 months of essential expenses, in a renewable term deposit or a money-market fund.
nucleo-pais-cl-dica-2 = APV: under regime B the contribution comes off the tax base (up to 600 UF a year); under regime A the state adds 15%.
nucleo-pais-cl-dica-3 = Compare your AFP's fee: the gap between the cheapest and the most expensive weighs on retirement.
nucleo-pais-cl-limite-1 = The Impuesto Único uses the October 2026 UTM and contributions use the average AFP fee (1.1%).
nucleo-pais-cl-limite-2 = The legal gratificación counts as part of the monthly salary you enter.

## Other countries (generic mode)

nucleo-pais-outro-dica-1 = An emergency fund of 3 to 6 months of essential spending, somewhere safe that you can withdraw from quickly.
nucleo-pais-outro-dica-2 = Set your savings aside on payday and track your spending by category.
nucleo-pais-outro-dica-3 = Compare your investments with the country's inflation and the central bank's reference interest rate.
nucleo-pais-outro-limite-1 = Salary deductions (taxes and social security) aren't calculated: enter the net amount or import the payslip.
nucleo-pais-outro-limite-2 = Data sources, taxes and screens that only apply to Brazil are turned off.

